config NOCFREE_BLE_PROFILE_NAME
    bool "Append the Bluetooth profile number to the advertised device name"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_BLE && BT_DEVICE_NAME_DYNAMIC
    # Central only. The ZMK calls it makes are not compiled into a split
    # peripheral, where it would fail at link time -- so the right half gets
    # this module on its module list too, and it simply switches itself off.
    depends on !ZMK_SPLIT || ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL
    help
      ZMK advertises one static name for every profile, so five profiles all
      appear to a host as the same device and there is no way to tell which
      slot you are pairing. The factory firmware names them per slot. This
      renames on every profile change, matching that convention.
